    "debrief":  {
                    "realTeam":  "Spirit and Opportunity had no way to clean their solar panels. As dust piled up, their power slowly dropped. Then, in March 2005, gusts of wind blew most of the dust off Spirit\u0027s panels and its power jumped way up. The team was amazed! These wind \u0027cleaning events\u0027 helped both rovers keep working for years longer than planned.",
                    "tryNext":  "Clean the panels when they pass about 40% dust, and make each trip outside short so you save air.",
                    "realScience":  {
                                        "title":  "Dust devils",
                                        "text":  "A dust devil is a spinning column of warm air that lifts dust. On Mars they can be taller than a mountain. Orbiters have photographed their dark tracks crossing the ground.",
